    <summary>Restore old photos offline with local photo restoration software: it cleans damaged photos from scanned prints, reconstructs faces and colorizes black and white photos, with batch mode and an 8x enlarger.</summary>
    <description>SoftOrbits Photo Retoucher is digital photo restoration software for Windows that cleans scanned prints so you can restore old photos on the local machine. The package is meant for old photo restoration in libraries, local history archives and photo studios, where several digitizing stations process donated or customer prints without sending them to an online service.

![Photo Retoucher screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/ret/ret-v1-main.png)

## Setting up the photo retouching software

On first launch the program asks to download its AI models. Approve it on each workstation and let the download complete before handing the PC to staff. A CUDA-capable graphics card speeds things up, and machines without one run the same functions on the processor.

The same install also serves as photo retouching software for newer pictures: you can enhance photos with manual brightness, contrast and saturation controls and an AI enlarger that scales small scans up to 8x before they go to print.

## How to use the digital photo restoration software

1. Load a scan of the damaged photo in TIFF, PNG, JPEG or a RAW format.
2. Start the AI restoration with one click. The software recovers faces and fixes blur, grain and surface damage, keeping each person's expression. On badly damaged prints fine details may differ from the original photo.
3. Decide whether to colorize a black and white photo or leave it monochrome, then correct single colors manually if the AI picked the wrong shade.
4. Erase handwritten dates, stamps, watermarks or stray objects with the Object Remover, and clean any leftovers with the Clone Stamp.
5. For a full box of prints, batch mode is the key feature: set it up with only the steps you need and process them in one run, or run face retouching alone.

Trial note: staff can test every repair step in the free trial and compare before and after, yet an unregistered copy will not write the restored picture to a file. Activating a license allows saving.

![Photo Retoucher screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/ret/ret-v1-ai.png)

## Who uses it for old photo restoration, from beginners to pros

- Archives and libraries digitizing donated collections of faded photos.
- Photo studios that repair customer prints in poor condition with digital photo restoration software.
- Genealogy volunteers who restore old family photos of ancestors.
- Anyone who wants to remove scratches from photos without retouching each one by hand.

![Photo Retoucher screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/ret/ret-v1-result.png)

## Trial and license

This package installs the free trial of Photo Retoucher, commercial photo restoration software by SoftOrbits. Full use, including saving restored images, requires a paid license. Plans, including a business license: [Photo Retoucher](https://www.softorbits.net/old-photo-restoration-software/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package).

[SoftOrbits Photo Retoucher on Windows Store](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9MWTL7ZFKS0V)

## FAQ

### How can I restore a damaged old photo?

Start from the sharpest scan of the original photo you can make, because a detailed scan gives the AI more to work with. Run the automatic repair first and use the manual tools only for what is left.

### How much does it cost to restore an old photo?

With this photo restoration software there is no fee per picture, since one license covers every photo you process. The trial is free to evaluate, and current prices are on the product site.

### Where can I get my old photos restored?

You can do old photo restoration yourself at home or at work with a scanner and this photo software, which keeps the prints and the files in your hands. For a large collection, batch mode handles a whole folder.
